lingmo-wine (1.0.2+lingmo5u1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Launch EXE/MSI files directly on double-click, automatically initialize or
    reuse their environment, and provide Lingmo default MIME associations.
  * Edit application entries, remove and undo launcher registration, and
    preserve launcher IDs when registering an existing program.
  * Add environment renaming, initialized state, folder and installed EXE
    selection, and bounded per-environment log viewing.
  * Guard busy input and async selection state; add runtime and management
    integration regression tests.

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:02:08 +0800

lingmo-wine (1.0.1+lingmo5u1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add shared action state, global menus and compact local fallback.
  * Fill the window header width so close, minimize and maximize are visible.
  * Use a glass navigation sidebar and opaque content with separate install,
    application, environment and log pages. Preserve input across page switches.
  * Test window button bounds and clicking Close at multiple sizes and scales.

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:58:00 +0800

lingmo-wine (1.0.0+lingmo5u1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial SDK-based Wine environment manager and on-demand runner.
  * Add EXE/MSI file association, per-application launchers, and runtime tests.

